ch the program's CP1251 output byte-for-byte as substrings. Since tests are green, they do.\n\nWait — but actually there IS a potential encoding issue. The program output goes through redirection `> file`. In MSVC, when stdout is redirected to a file, is it text mode (with CRLF translation)? Yes, by default stdout is text mode. So `\\n` → `\\r\\n`. The expect files have CRLF (we saw 0D 0A in the hexdump). So they match. Good.\n\nBut hold on: `std::print` writes to stdout via the C++ stream. In text mode, `\\n` is translated to `\\r\\n`. Yes.\n\n22. **The `t3_empty_case` expect content — is it the same for C and C++?** Yes, shared expect file, both programs produce identical message. Good.\n\n23. **Check `t3_not_digit_case` expect (36 bytes):** \"Строка 1. Нечисловое данное: 3 2 bam\". Wait, C++ main.cpp says \"Нечисловое данное:\" (line 42: `\"������ %d. ���������� ������: %s\\n\"`). Let me decode: \"Строка 1. Нечисловое данное: 3 2 bam\"? Actually C++ line 42: `std::cerr << \"������ \" << i << \". ���������� ������: \" << temp << \"\\n\";`. The garbled text \"���������� ������\" = \"Нечисловое данное\"? Hmm. And C main.c line 69: `fprintf(stderr, \"������ %d. ���������� ������: %s\\n\", i, s);` — same message. Good, consistent.\n\nLet me verify the expect file content decodes properly. Earlier cat showed t3_not_digit_case = \"��ப� 1. ���᫮�� �����: 3 2 bam\". As CP1251 read as... the console mangled it. Fine, tests pass.\n\n24. **`t3_too_few_args_case` expect (51 bytes):** C++ line 39: `\"������ %d. ��������� ���������� X Y Z. ��������: %s\\n\"` → \"Строка 1. Не хватает координат X Y Z. Найдено: 2 3\". 51 bytes. Count: \"Строка 1. Не хватает координат X Y Z. Найдено: 2 3\": Строка(6)+sp(1)+1(1)+.(1)+sp(1) = 10; \"Не\"(2)+sp(1)+\"хватает\"(7)+sp(1)+\"координат\"(9)+sp(1) = 21 → 31; \"X\"(1)+sp(1)+\"Y\"(1)+sp(1)+\"Z\"(1)+.(1)+sp(1) = 7 → 38; \"Найдено\"(7)+:(1)+sp(1) = 9 → 47; \"2\"(1)+sp(1)+\"3\"(1) = 3 → 50. Hmm 50, file is 51. Extra byte = trailing newline? If resu