 line 39-42 shows \"нечисловое данное\". And C main.c line 69: `\"Строка %d. Нечисловое данное: %s\\n\"`. OK.\n\nWait, but is \"данное\" correct? The message \"Строка 1. Нечисловое данное: 3 2 bam\" — hmm, could be \"данное\" or \"данные\". Let me decode carefully:\nCD E5 F7 E8 F1 EB EE E2 FB E5 = \"Нечисловое\" (Н-е-ч-и-с-л-о-в-о-е)\n20 = space\nE4 E0 ED ED FB E5 = \"данное\" (д-а-н-н-о-е)\nSo \"Нечисловое данное\". OK.\n\nt3_too_few_args_case: D1 F2 F0 EE EA E0 20 31 2E 20 CE E6 E8 E4 E0 EB E8 F1 FC 20 EA EE EE F0 E4 E8 ED E0 F2 FB 20 58 20 59 20 5A 2E 20 CF EE EB F3 F7 E5 ED EE 3A 20 32 20 33\n= \"Строка 1. Ожидалось координаты X Y Z. Получено: 2 3\"\nCE=О, E6=ж, E8=и, E4=д, E0=а, EB=л, E8=и, F1=с, FC=ь\n\"Ожидалось\" — hmm wait. C main.c line 62: `\"Строка %d. Ожидалось координат X Y Z. Найдено: %s\\n\"`? Let me check. Actually earlier in main.c: `fprintf(stderr, \"Строка %d. Ожидалось координат X Y Z. Найдено: %s\\n\", i, s);` Hmm, but the bytes say \"Получено:\". Let me decode:\nCF EE EB F3 F7 E5 ED EE 3A 20 = \"Получено: \" (П-о-л-у-ч-е-н-о-:)\nSo message is \"Строка 1. Ожидалось координаты X Y Z. Получено: 2 3\".\n\nHmm wait, need to double check C++ vs C message consistency since both use same expect files. Let me check what C++ main.cpp prints for too few. main.cpp line 39: `\"Строка %d. Ожидалось координаты X Y Z. Получено: %s\\n\"`. And C main.c line 62: same? Both shared expect file t3_too_few_args_case. Since tests pass, they must match. OK.\n\nNow, there's a subtle issue. The t3_too_few_args_case input is \"2 3\" (3 bytes: \"2 3\", no trailing newline? Length 3, so \"2 3\"). The C version: parse_point... For C version, \"2 3\" - the get_string reads until newline, but there's no newline at EOF. Earlier there was a bug about EOF handling. The expect says \"Получено: 2 3\" - no trailing space. But wait, in the bat file the C version expected \"2 3 \" with a trailing space (from journal: `findstr /C:\"Строка 1. Ожидалось координаты X Y Z. Получено: 2 3 \"`). Hmm, the expect file now has \"2 3\" without trailing space. And check_contains does substring matching: result must contain expected. If C program outputs \"Получено: 2 3 \\n\" (with trailing space), the substring \"Получено: 2 3\" still matches. So it passes either way. OK.\n\nNow let me think about the main review points. Let me list issues I've found:\n\n1. **Line 58-59: `COMMON_CPP_DLL_OBJ` and `COMMON_C_DLL_OBJ` are defined but never used.** They're duplicated by `CPP_DLL_OBJ` (line 215) and `C_DLL_OBJ` (line 219). Dead code. This is the \"повторила дважды — выноси\" / dead code issue. Should remove.\n\n2. **Line 71: commented out `T3_CPP_OBJ`** - leftover comment, \"закомментированные блоки\" policy (§4.1.10). Should remove.\n\n3. **`GEN_CLOUD` is defined and built but never used in tests.** The task (§6.1) requires mass tests with gen_cloud for t3: \"Массовый вход (задачи 3–4): генератор облака точек gen_cloud --size --seed, размеры 10 / 100 / 10⁶; данные в build/ под .gitignore.\" But the Makefile doesn't have any mass tests for t3 using gen_cloud. So the mass tests are missing. This is a real gap vs the task spec. But maybe the user intends mass tests to be added later, or maybe she considers current scope. I should flag this.\n\n4. **Independent reference (эталон) policy**: §4.9.3 says etalon computed by independent reference implementation (for t3-t4: PowerShell однострочник or separate simple exe). Currently t3 tests use `tests\\expect\\t3_test1` etc. — frozen snapshot files. Wait, the policy says \"Замороженный снапшот выхода — не эталон корректности\". But for the small literal tests (t3_test1/2/3), these are hand-crafted short literals, not \"frozen snapshot of program output\". The §6.1 says \"вход — от генератора или короткий литерал; эталон — независимая референс-реализация на лету\". Hmm. For t3 the bat tests used findstr with hardcoded substrings. The Makefile now uses check_contains with expect files. \n\nActually wait — the mass tests are