lure mode. Fix: prereq lib instead of (or in addition to) dll. With grouped targets, prereq on lib: lib missing → group rule fires → both rebuilt. \n\nBut is depending on dll ALSO still needed? For runtime tests, PATH covers dll. For build, only lib needed. So replacing dll→lib is enough for build. But the dll-prereq also ensured dll freshly built before tests... if lib is rebuilt, dll is rebuilt too (group). So lib prereq suffices. I'll recommend changing prereq from common_cpp.dll to common_cpp.lib. Actually to be safe against \"dll manually deleted\" I could suggest both. I'll present the tradeoff.\n\nClaim C (dead code): verified lines 58-59 unused (only CPP_DLL_OBJ/C_DLL_OBJ used at 215/219). Line 71 commented T3_CPP_OBJ unused. Remove.\n\nClaim D (header deps): dll obj rules (185-195) list only .cpp, not .hpp/.h. Static obj rules (172-182) list both. Inconsistent. Real risk: change geometry.hpp → dll not rebuilt → stale. Fix: add headers to dll obj prereqs.\n\nClaim A (mass tests): gen_cloud built but not referenced as prereq anywhere → never built in `make all`/`make test`. Confirmed via grep (GEN_CLOUD only in def + rule). Mass tests missing entirely. This is the biggest gap vs §6.1.\n\nAlso flag: README §\"make test\" still says \"для t1-t2\" (line 66) — outdated, should mention t3. And README make all says \"t1-t2\" (line 64). Minor doc staleness. And t3_build_and_test.bat now redundant (transition-script policy) — but only after mass tests move to make.\n\nAlso the gitignore of ref ps1: §4.9.3 says reference source should be in repo. Flag as question.\n\nLet me write this up now. Since I'm in plan mode, I'll present the review + proposed plan and ask for decisions. Keep it in Russian. Mark ФАКТ/МНЕНИЕ and confidence per the anti-sycophancy protocol.\n\nI should be careful not to overwhelm. Organize by severity with clear file:line references.\n\nLet me verify line numbers once more for the key items:\n- 58-59: COMMON_CPP_DLL_OBJ / COMMON_C_DLL_OBJ (unused